WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.878
Experiments gone wrong, snake wieners, and

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:09.920
actual footage of me getting a sponge bath. Episode 2 of Lovecraft Country is here with all new theories and details to break down.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.120
In this video we'll be diving into the mystery behind Atticus's true ancestry Artem's secret

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.680
society and don't even get me started on how adorable these baby shohgoths are.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.840
But before we begin show me some love by hitting that like button and

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.760
subscribing so you can get notified as soon as one of my breakdowns comes out.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.559
Well, it didn't take long for George and Letti to get over their traumatic experience with the shogoths.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.200
That's because their memory of the event has been wiped. At the end of episode 1 we heard a whistle

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.040
which was used to call off the shogoths.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.700
But this whistle also did that "Men in Black" thing and they have no recollection of those bloodthirsty

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:51.599
monsters. This mysterious Artem mansion just so happens to have tons of clothes for Letti to try on and all of George's favorite books.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:58.200
It's as if whoever wants them there wants them to stay. A particular note are the favorite authors George recounts.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:05.260
Algernon Blackwood,  William Hodgson, and Clark Ashton Smith. All of them are contemporaries of H.P

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:10.580
Lovecraft; who Lovecraft himself praised. In fact William Hodgson's book "The House on the Borderlands,"

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.280
makes an appearance later on in the episode. A book written in 1908 about a man's

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.879
hallucinatory account of a remote house and his experiences with

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.799
supernatural creatures and other dimensions. Sounds familiar.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.199
While Letti and George can't seem to remember what happened the previous night, Atticus ¹

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:34.799
does. He seems to be impervious to the whistle's memory wiping power. Likely because he has the blood of Titus Braithwaite flowing through him.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.599
But we'll get to that in a bit. As resident "Children of Corn," William leads them to lunch,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.559
we pass a few interesting paintings. This is John

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:48.959
Trumbull's 1839 painting, "The Last Family," who perished in the deluge. Depicting a family washed out to sea

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.560
foreshadowing the deaths of two characters later in the episode.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.299
The second is Renault's

00:01:54.299 --> 00:02:01.359
1795 painting "The Genius of France Between Liberty and Death." Depicting an angel in between a lady liberty on the left and

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.520
death on the right. Our captives are stuck in a similar dilemma to this angel.

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:12.559
Held captive, deprived of their liberty on the one hand and the spector of death on the other. Atticus wants to find his father

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.000
but according to William, he's on an errand and won't be back till later.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.679
They get a tour of this creepy mansion and its founder Titus Braithwaite.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.720
Fun fact, braith comes from the old Irish word for betrayer. Notice here this ring, a

00:02:24.879 --> 00:02:28.159
symbol of The Order of the Ancient Dawn, the secret society

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:33.459
we'll learn more about in a bit. Titus apparently made his fortune in shipping. Which Letti surmises

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:40.640
involved the shipping of slaves. As we'll learn later Titus did own slaves impregnating one named Hannah who happens to be a

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.800
great-great-grandmother of Atticus. They decide to check out the village of Artem

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.759
which looks like it's run by the Amish. But find on their way their car, which was completely destroyed

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:56.239
the other night is totally repaired. Notice how Artem utilizes a lot of red. From the barn to the flowers

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.560
to the kids playing whatever the hell this is.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:05.440
It's all to foreshadow danger. Atticus hears a whistle blown, the same sound he heard that called off the shogoths the previous night.

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:12.799
It was blown by this woman who holds sway over this creepy stone silo. A silo Atticus believes may hold his father.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:17.039
It's important to note that the whistle is what makes Letti and George lose their memory.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:22.879
But Atticus is impervious to it. On their way back to the manor as if they didn't learn anything from the previous night,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:30.080
they're saved from another attack by none other than Christina Braithwaite. The daughter of Samuel Braithwaite who we'll meet in a bit.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:36.158
Atticus is taken to Samuel's lab where Samuel's own organs are being harvested for a dinner later in the evening.

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:38.720
It's okay

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.319
however, since Samuel has the ability to heal. Healing Letti near the end of the episode after shooting her. Here

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:50.720
we learn of a painting based off a biblical verse in the book of Genesis. This  painting however was not painted by a Joseph

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.879
Tanhauser as Samuel suggests.

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:58.239
It's by John Miles and it's called, "The Naming of the Animals," in which Adam helps God in creation by

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:03.039
creating a beautiful hierarchy of all living things. That no good Eve arrived

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:03.519
however

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:07.599
and tempted Adam. Throwing the hierarchy into a mess of tribes and nations.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.000
Now Samuel here believes he can find a way back to the garden of Eden where things are

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.059
perfect, and he can be immortal. He needs however Tick's power. The blood of his ancestors.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:24.499
Christina locks Tick in his room with a spell. Tick will later communicate with George through the walls using morse code calling their captors

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.679
Wizards. We'll also get this super odd scene where Christina delivers a baby shogoth from a cow.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.320
I'm still scratching my head as to why this scene was put in here as it really doesn't advance the story.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:40.479
But it's possible the writers are setting something up and need us to know that these normal animals are being used as vessels for

00:04:40.699 --> 00:04:43.599
abominable horrors that can later be controlled by Christina.

00:04:43.759 --> 00:04:47.759
I think we definitely haven't seen the last of her. Tick, George, and Letti all experience

00:04:48.139 --> 00:04:55.439
hallucinations as part of this secret society's evening entertainment. Letti makes out with a hallucination of Atticus only to find he's got a snake penis.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.199
We get this shot of Adam and Eve. Adam here also having a snake penis

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:05.280
and some have interpreted this story from the bible as the snake symbolizing Satan and the forbidden fruit as

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:10.720
insemination. I didn't learn that in Sunday school! George is visited by Dora his brother's wife.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:17.839
It's really hinted here that Dora and him had an affair and that this affair resulted in the birth of Atticus. Making George

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.959
Atticus's real father. George even tells Montrose that Atticus is probably not his kid.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:28.320
Something the two of them apparently settled years ago. Further proof of this is when George tells Dora about a story

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:34.879
he's writing involving a man who reunites with his long lost love. And they stayed together before a house collapses on them.

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:42.719
And what happens at the end of this episode? A house collapses and George dies. Allowing him to finally be reunited with his long-lost love

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:50.479
Dora who died before him. The final hallucination occurs between Tick and Ji-ha. Remember that girl Tick called from Korea last episode?

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.479
That's her. She's also that red alien thing that appeared in his dreams.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:06:00.079
She is really pissed at him and I can't help but think that her anger is directly related to the bad things

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.560
Atticus said he did while fighting in Korea.

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:07.359
We aren't exactly sure what those bad things are yet, but we'll likely find those out in future episodes.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:15.039
It's really interesting to note here that in the subtitles, it says that Ji-ha isn't speaking Korean, but quote "the language of Adam."

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.979
This is also the language she probably spoke to him in episode one.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.919
But I don't speak Korean so I can't be 100 percent sure. Later in the episode,

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:29.039
Christina says the language of Adam is so tricky that men have died trying to wield its power.

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:35.519
I am wondering if the book Hannah escapes with at the end of the episode contains more information about this powerful language.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.359
This is likely what George called "The Book of Names," or "The Book of Life."

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:43.999
It's the opposite of "The Book of the Dead: the Necronomicon." Tick and George are invited to dinner.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:50.479
Sorry Letti, its boys only.  No girls allowed. There George recites the laws of their ancient order in a book

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:55.199
He found called, "Bylaws and Precepts of the Order of the Ancient Dawn." By their own law

00:06:55.360 --> 00:07:02.400
regular members must obey orders from those deemed Sons among Sons; those who are direct descendants of Titus Braithwaite.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.639
And since Atticus is the last blood heir he orders everyone to go home.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:13.120
So Atticus, Letti, and George head back to that silo where they find Montrose having just escaped. And if you're looking for some nice

00:07:13.259 --> 00:07:15.519
tear-felt reunion between father and son

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.919
you ain't gonna get it. As they make their escape in that silver sedan from episode 1

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.120
we learn that this particular lodge is one of many in a much larger secret society.

00:07:25.199 --> 00:07:30.639
This one is called "The Sons of Adam," and years ago they failed at conjuring a spell of immortality

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:35.119
which killed everyone inside except of course Hannah. Their escape is short-lived

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:35.520
however

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:40.479
when they smash headfirst into a force field. To make matters worse Samuel shoots Letti and

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:46.319
George. He ends up healing Letti to prove to Atticus that he can heal but won't heal George until he gets

00:07:46.539 --> 00:07:49.359
Atticus's help with his spell. Sponge bath time!

00:07:49.599 --> 00:07:56.639
Christina tells Atticus of Samuel's master plan to open a portal to Eden and there's a lot of talk about changing destiny and even

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.519
a social commentary on how Atticus was made a member

00:07:59.759 --> 00:08:06.079
solely based on his sex while Christina can never be a member because she's a woman. I think this is setting up her character arc

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:12.079
since Samuel dies at the end, I'm wondering if she'll try to take over. While George is on his deathbed we learn a bit more

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:12.699
about

00:08:12.699 --> 00:08:20.079
Montrose's past. He was beaten by his father for liking to draw. Montrose would later go on to beat Atticus for his love of books.

00:08:20.319 --> 00:08:25.519
It's a sad but revelatory bit of information showing how trauma and abuse can pass from one

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:31.120
generation to the next. As Atticus is forced to perform in this experiment, a slave to his situation

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.799
just like his ancestors were actual slaves to theirs, Gil

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:40.180
Scott Heron's poem, "Whitey on the Moon" plays. A poem which depicts the plight of African Americans

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.560
uable to pay medical bills and rent,

00:08:42.719 --> 00:08:47.119
when the government is spending millions of their tax dollars on sending white folks to the moon.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:50.319
We are seeing Samuel's experiment at the expense of a black man

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:55.360
just like the progress of space advancement was at the expense of millions of Black Americans.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.279
This sentiment is also found in James Baldwin's speech from episode 1.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:05.119
If you haven't checked out my video on that I'll leave a link in the description. As the experiment progresses a portal opens with

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:08.879
garden-like flowers suggesting the garden of Eden is on the other side.

00:09:08.959 --> 00:09:14.879
But before the experiment goes completely haywire, just like it did decades ago, Atticus sees his great ancestor

00:09:14.959 --> 00:09:21.518
Hannah visibly pregnant on the other side. We also see this black smoke-like essence emanate from Atticus's ring.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.880
This seems to be the energy that turns the others into stone.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.920
But why it comes out of the ring and why it didn't turn Atticus into stone remains to be seen.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.399
We do know that it was Charlotte who gave him this ring. Leading me to believe she played a role in sabotaging her father's plan

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:43.760
as retribution for keeping her on the sidelines her entire life because she's a woman. I also just really enjoyed the

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:49.839
juxtaposition of Atticus and his great ancestor escaping the home as it's destroyed in their respective times.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.000
But even though Atticus makes it out alive

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:57.039
he finds out his uncle has passed, leaving us wondering what the heck will happen next. Now

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:00.719
there is an episode 3 preview which I've left a link to in the description below.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:06.799
But even after watching that, I'm still scratching my head what the whole series is working towards. Thanks for watching everyone.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:07.460
Please make sure to like and subscribe. I'm planning on breaking down every episode of the series.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:12.600
I'm also interested to hear your thoughts in the comments below. You can also follow me on twitter at thinkstoryyt

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.500
Until next time remember daddy loves you very much.

